From: Minori IKEDA <daisy19@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] tab: include <sys/wait.h> for the wait status macros

src/ptyxis-tab.c uses WIFEXITED, WEXITSTATUS, WIFSIGNALED and WTERMSIG but
never includes <sys/wait.h>.  POSIX places those macros in that header; the
file builds on glibc only because another header happens to pull it in.

On systems whose headers follow the POSIX placement more strictly the file
does not compile.  This was hit both by the OpenBSD port and while porting
Ptyxis to MIU Darwin, which suggests the include is genuinely missing rather
than either system being unusual.

The include is harmless where the macros already arrive by another route.
---
 src/ptyxis-tab.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/src/ptyxis-tab.c
+++ b/src/ptyxis-tab.c
@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@
 #include <glib/gi18n.h>

 #include <cairo.h>
+#include <sys/wait.h>

 #ifdef __linux__
 # include <libportal/portal.h>
